0.4877582788467407,-2.706014311115723e-05,-0.31217142939567566,-0.0030830015894025564,-3.576278118089249e-07,-0.9773010015487671,-0.3264997601509094,-0.0005902693956159055,0.0,0.0,-2.3841855067985307e-07,0.0,0.0,0.0,-0.3003949820995331,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-7.510157047363464e-06,-0.012586444616317749,0.0,-0.0056998105719685555,-0.0002520958660170436,-0.0013162767281755805,-9.536738616588991e-07],"request":{"active_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,32,501,6176,5440,646,387,10275,304,697,2114,369,264,825,7246,13713,2783,315,57960,3,16,15,26266,0,15,15,15,3,323,9775,13404,7049,315,57960,3,21,20,15,3,817,1042,13,1416,279,6176,5440,374,9966,311,3581,498,57960,3,16,17,15,15,3,1817,1042,304,4802,18610,11,1246,1657,4361,1635,686,432,1896,311,51521,349,697,7049,30,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nA new green technology can be installed in your home for a one-time installation cost of $\\$10,\\!000$ and annual maintenance costs of $\\$650$ per year. If the green technology is supposed to save you $\\$1200$ each year in energy bills, how many whole years will it take to recuperate your costs?","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"e9b9c1e80ef65ab9a447315c3a562ab5a55a3cb32267b064fe80446496470ee4"},"seconds":8.988415479660034,"seed":817356387433814623,"stop":"eos","text":"To determine how many whole years it will take to recuperate the costs of the green technology, we need to calculate the total savings over time and compare it to the initial installation cost plus the maintenance costs.\n\nLet's denote the number of years by \\( n \\).\n\n1. **Initial Installation Cost**: \\$10,000\n2. **Annual Maintenance Cost**: \\$650\n3. **Annual Savings**: \\$1200\n\nThe total cost after \\( n \\) years, including the initial installation cost and the maintenance costs, is:\n\\[ \\text{Total Cost} = 10000 + 650n \\]\n\nThe total savings after \\( n \\) years is:\n\\[ \\text{Total Savings} = 1200n \\]\n\nTo find the number of years it takes to recuperate the costs, we set the total cost equal to the total savings:\n\\[ 10000 + 650n = 1200n \\]\n\nNow, solve for \\( n \\):\n\\[ 10000 = 1200n - 650n \\]\n\\[ 10000 = 550n \\]\n\\[ n = \\frac{10000}{550} \\]\n\\[ n = \\frac{1000}{55} \\]\n\\[ n \\approx 18.18 \\]\n\nSince we need the number of whole years, we round up to the next whole number because even a fraction of a year means the cost will not be fully recovered until the next full year.\n\nTherefore, it will take \\( \\boxed{19} \\) whole years to recuperate the costs."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{19}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"algebra:1018"}
